  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Given name first, then the family name, and most people have a middle name too. Family names come from everywhere: English, Irish, German, Italian, Polish and Jewish names among white Americans; mostly English family names among Black Americans, who often carry modern or distinctive first names. Latinos in the US usually go by the father's surname alone (Maria Hernandez), though some keep both. Chinese, Korean, Vietnamese and Filipino Americans very often have an English first name, with the heritage name kept as a middle name or used at home (Kevin Nguyen, Grace Kim). Vietnamese and Korean names are written in Western order here, given name first.",
